<title>USA: G-III says revolving credit extended.</title>
<headline>G-III says revolving credit extended.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>G-III Apparel Group said Monday its lending group has extended its revolving credit agreement for two years through May 31, 1999.</p>
<p>The lending group consists of Fleet Financial Group Inc, Chase Manhattan Corp and CIT Group Holdings Inc which is jointly owned by Dai-Ichi Kangyo Bank Ltd and Chase Manhattan.</p>
<p>The agreement provides for a maximum credit facility of $52 million.</p>
<p>G-III is a manufacturer and distributor of leather and non-leather outerwear apparel.</p>
</text>
